{#- The composition of a structured turn's message (FR-RESP-8, FR-RATE-4; #152).

The polish pass: the turn's verified beats, as the output viewpoint receives them, joined into
one message. The ``system`` block holds the rating guidance (always first, FR-RATE-4), the
custom instructions and the rules of composition; the ``user`` block lists each beat (its
index, kind, actor and text) and their deterministic assembly as the draft. The answer is the
call's ``response_schema`` (``{text}``). The engine checks it (claim detection, traceability,
attribution, no private thought) and releases the draft instead when it fails. -#}
{% macro line(entry) -%}
{% if entry.text %}{{ entry.text }}{% else %}{{ entry.name }}:{% if entry.say %} "{{ entry.say }}"{% endif %}{% if entry.do %} *{{ entry.do }}*{% endif %}{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}
{% block system %}
{% if rating_guidance %}
## Content rating guidance
{{ rating_guidance }}

{% endif %}
{% if custom_instructions %}
## Custom instructions
{{ custom_instructions }}

{% endif %}
## Composition
Join the beats below into one message for the reader, in their order. You may smooth the prose and add short connective stage text, nothing more:
- every line keeps the words and the speaker its beat gives it: never move a line to someone else, never change who does what;
- add no fact, event, object, place, number or time that no beat states;
- leave out no beat.
{% if composition_omniscient %}
- a thought keeps its label, written as `[Name thinks] …`, and a hidden fact as `[latent] …`.
{% else %}
- the reader cannot see anyone's thoughts: do not describe what a character thinks, feels inside or knows privately.
{% endif %}
Answer with the message as `text`.
{% endblock %}
{% block user %}
## Beats
{% for b in composition_beats %}
[{{ b.index }}] {{ b.kind }}{% if b.name %} — {{ b.name }}{% endif %}: {{ b.text }}
{% endfor %}

## Draft
<draft>
{{ composition_draft }}
</draft>
{% endblock %}
